"""hydrocron_standalone: PO.DAAC's Hydrocron SWOT river time series as
one self-contained MCP tool.

This file exists to be LIFTED. It imports nothing from any other file
in this repository: fetch, parse, error handling, an embedded test
fixture, and the offline test all live here, so an engineer at the
archive can fork this single file and own the surface outright. The
same tool also ships inside the broader observations server; this
copy is the separable artifact backing that promise.

CONTRACT (matching the observations server v0.2 conventions):
successful responses carry retrieved_at, request_url, server_version;
long series keep the TAIL and name the returned time span; failures
return structured {"error", "source", "status", "detail"} with the
agency's own message, never a bare exception.

WHAT LEAVES YOUR MACHINE: the feature type, feature id, time range,
and field list, over HTTPS to PO.DAAC's Hydrocron endpoint. The API
is anonymous; no credential exists in this process.

Run: uv run hydrocron_standalone.py            (stdio MCP server)
     uv run hydrocron_standalone.py --selftest (one live probe)
     uv run hydrocron_standalone.py --test     (offline, embedded fixture)
"""
from __future__ import annotations

import datetime as dt
import json
import sys
import time

import httpx
from mcp.server.mcpserver import MCPServer

VERSION = "0.1.0"
UA = {"User-Agent": f"hydrocron-standalone-mcp/{VERSION}"}
MAX_ROWS = 500
ENDPOINT = ("https://soto.podaac.earthdatacloud.nasa.gov/hydrocron/v1/"
            "timeseries")
mcp = MCPServer("hydrocron")

